From 9c7d1941e55f3d5fb7b9e22442d6e7f7d664e518 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Han <danielhanchen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:47:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] FP8 block dequant on gfx11 ROCm: ragged / rectangular e4m3fn
 blocks take the byte decoder

On gfx1151 (RDNA 3.5) the cases the chunked torch loop takes (ragged or rectangular blocks, and
even tiles when Triton has no fp8e4nv) run the one-pass e4m3fn byte decoder instead, which is
bit-identical to the torch loop for bf16 / fp32 output. fp16 output keeps the torch loop, and
even tiles keep the fp8e4nv kernel. Other ROCm archs (CDNA, RDNA2, gfx12, gfx950) are unchanged.
UNSLOTH_FP8_HIP_BYTES_DEQUANT=0 restores the old routes. NVIDIA routing is unchanged.
---
